1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
A planet is orbiting its star backwards. And tilted.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:09,000
Our planets all orbit the way the Sun spins

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,500
GJ 3090 b, 73 light-years away, around a red dwarf

4
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:18,000
About 2.2 times Earth's radius, 4.5 times its mass

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:22,500
One orbit takes 2.9 days

6
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:27,000
Orbit tilted about 136 degrees: past sideways, into backwards

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,000
The first retrograde planet found around a red dwarf

8
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,000
No known companion to explain it. Why comes next

9
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Yann Carteret, University of Geneva. NIRPS, La Silla, Chile
